From: Rain Valentine <rsg000@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 17:04:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/8] Unit tests: run the fast path suites' server init once
 per process

Port of the audit's test_server_init.hpp (Phase 8 hygiene commits
9bb1b64bb, 8e57486a0, d050192b4, 6a6febe14 and e36c2baab) and its use
in the fixtures of FastpathExecutorTest, FastpathStagedTest and
AclOffloadTest.

Each of these suites brings up part of the server in SetUpTestSuite with
moduleInitModulesSystem, populateCommandTable, ACLInit and
connTypeInitialize. Those functions run once per process: a second call
blocks forever on the module GIL (moduleInitModulesSystem leaves it
locked), aborts in commandAddSubcommand, breaks the ACL category table,
or asserts in connTypeRegister. On this branch the gtest binary therefore
hangs as soon as two of these suites run in one process, for example
./valkey-unit-gtests --gtest_filter='FastpathExecutorTest.*:FastpathStagedTest.*'
or --gtest_repeat=2 on one suite (checked on c8b06eb0f: both time out).
gtest-parallel hides this by running one test per process.

The helpers make the second and later calls safe (release the GIL and
close the old module pipe, re-add the already filled command table to
the new hashtables, register connection types and ACL categories once).
The fixtures also delete their event loop at suite end so its epoll fd
is not leaked per iteration.

FastpathStagedTest.LanesWillRunCountsEachSegment used INCR as the
command that is not a lane command. fpMarkLaneCommands marks the lane
commands once per process, so after any suite that ran write lanes INCR
is a lane command and the test fails. It now uses SETBIT, which is never
a lane command.

With this the eight fast path, poller, replication and ACL suites run
together in one process, shuffled and repeated 8 times, with no
failure.

Signed-off-by: Rain Valentine <rsg000@gmail.com>
